Install the generated itk_expat.h wrapper header so downstream consumers
that include <itk_expat.h> via gifti_io.h can find it. Upstream's
Modules/ThirdParty/Expat/CMakeLists.txt calls configure_file() to emit
the header into the build tree but never adds an install() rule —
gifti_io.h is installed to ITK-6.0/ and references itk_expat.h, so
without this patch every downstream FTBFS at:

  /usr/include/ITK-6.0/gifti_io.h:5:10: fatal error: itk_expat.h: No such file or directory

Affects ITK_USE_SYSTEM_EXPAT=ON AND OFF paths identically. Uses the
global ${ITK_INSTALL_INCLUDE_DIR} which is set by the build system
(per-module ITKExpat_INSTALL_INCLUDE_DIR isn't populated in this
CMakeLists context — that's only set inside src/CMakeLists.txt).

--- a/Modules/ThirdParty/Expat/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Modules/ThirdParty/Expat/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -42,4 +42,8 @@ endif()

 configure_file(src/itk_expat.h.in src/itk_expat.h)

+install(FILES ${ITKExpat_BINARY_DIR}/src/itk_expat.h
+        DESTINATION ${ITK_INSTALL_INCLUDE_DIR}
+        COMPONENT Development)
+
 itk_module_impl()
